{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqd9ezu3tu4","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gate error message misleads Claude Code: says \"create graph task\" when native TaskCreate is the right tool","summary":"Distinct from the session_id mismatch gate bug. This is a UX copy problem: main_session_deny_message() in hooks/orch-gate-trivial.sh tells agents \"Create a graph task then start_task\" but no MCP create_task tool exists in Claude Code harness — agents waste turns searching. Fix is one conditional in the shell function: if [ -n \"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID:-}\" ]; then print \"Use native TaskCreate tool, then dispatch a subagent that calls start_task (with session_id)\"; else keep existing message. Applies to both no_workers and default (*) cases. Task 1b609f88-d844-48df-943a-15aeb6ab202c/2 is the ready task holding this work.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T04:03:47.307Z","vec":[-0.07213766127824783,0.012975333258509636,-0.035457637161016464,-0.015839243307709694,-0.0278593972325325,-0.05735050514340401,0.03941512480378151,-0.01711590774357319,-0.03552180156111717,0.06770749390125275,0.0449773333966732,-0.07685381174087524,0.026694122701883316,0.051063232123851776,0.02440457046031952,0.035179272294044495,0.09231284260749817,-0.15181991457939148,0.0412563756108284,-0.0679490938782692,0.04678544029593468,-0.03581513464450836,0.012489103712141514,0.04960519075393677,-0.06093627214431763,-0.043309468775987625,-0.04415736719965935,-0.04232296720147133,0.04292172193527222,0.006565268617123365,0.020340608432888985,0.028108125552535057,-0.04031330719590187,-0.029262254014611244,0.13045218586921692,0.13791511952877045,-0.00039296605973504484,-0.015706781297922134,0.00308260228484869,-0.03366827219724655,-0.005807474721223116,-0.017331523820757866,-0.0554208979010582,0.03645705059170723,-0.016700364649295807,-0.014781356789171696,-0.06327249109745026,-0.02379206009209156,0.004819985944777727,-0.05758095532655716,0.013055468909442425,0.038484245538711